## TactiQ OS audit rules for the writable configuration on /data.
##
## Not in rules.d and not in audit.rules: these watches need their
## directories, which data-tactiq-dirs creates after sysinit, while
## audit.rules is loaded before it. On the first boot of a new device the
## directories do not exist yet when audit.rules loads, and a watch on a
## path whose parent is missing is refused. tactiq-audit-data-rules.service
## loads this file once they exist.
##
## No -D here: these rules add to the ones already loaded.

-w /data/site -p wa -k site-config
-w /data/tactiq/stop -p wa -k stop
